	<item>
		<title>By: Gayatri &#38; Abraham Hull</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=740&#038;cpage=1#comment-8559</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Gayatri &#38; Abraham Hull]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 27 Jun 2011 00:22:10 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=740#comment-8559</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Noor Nicolai was and is a true beacon of light. She was a true friend, a retreat guide and a Shefayat.
She left us her rhythmic zikr version of the first Sufi thought
&quot; There is only One God the eternal the only being none exists save S/he,&quot; and an Invocation song of Prophetesses with wazaif and a refrain honoring Uma Khaliq Allah, Mother of Creation and Uma Shaffee Allah, Mother of Healing.
Noor  &quot;Thy Light is in all forms, Thy Love in all beings, Hu Allah, Hu Allah, Hu Allah Hu.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Noor Nicolai was and is a true beacon of light. She was a true friend, a retreat guide and a Shefayat.<br />
She left us her rhythmic zikr version of the first Sufi thought<br />
&#8221; There is only One God the eternal the only being none exists save S/he,&#8221; and an Invocation song of Prophetesses with wazaif and a refrain honoring Uma Khaliq Allah, Mother of Creation and Uma Shaffee Allah, Mother of Healing.<br />
Noor  &#8220;Thy Light is in all forms, Thy Love in all beings, Hu Allah, Hu Allah, Hu Allah Hu.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: zaynab FitzPatrick</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=740&#038;cpage=1#comment-8109</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[zaynab FitzPatrick]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 05 May 2011 11:02:47 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=740#comment-8109</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Noor, true to her name, is a glorious light on the Path.  Noor was and continues to be a mentor and friend on the Path.  She showed us a way to walk through life and even through the shadow of the valley of death, with courage and balance.  Noor&#039;s radiant presence lives in our hearts.  She is a true friend.  Until we meet again, Bodhisattva, rest, peacefully rest.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Noor, true to her name, is a glorious light on the Path.  Noor was and continues to be a mentor and friend on the Path.  She showed us a way to walk through life and even through the shadow of the valley of death, with courage and balance.  Noor&#8217;s radiant presence lives in our hearts.  She is a true friend.  Until we meet again, Bodhisattva, rest, peacefully rest.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
